Recover a lost slash, and stop holding impossible memory candidates

The life box returned "5771577" and "677677" - 577/577 with the slash read
as a 1 or dropped - so no pair was found and every frame was refused. With
the maximum known, digits ending in exactly that maximum, with at most one
stray character where the slash was, now parse. Tokens that still contain a
slash are left to the normal pattern, so a phantom-digit maximum stays
refused.

Memory held sixteen components reading mana 0/32762, a sentinel rather than
a pool, because current-mana agreement was measured against the candidate's
own total. It is measured against the known maximum now, pools over three
times the known maximum are discarded, and a tie unbroken for a minute is
dropped and searched again.

